The `--step` surface of a `jinja: true` playbook renders the body through the context and then
appends the step lesson, whose own braces stay literal.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  fx_label: hermetic label
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_lessons/0002_step.md --
---
title: Step rule
targets: [fx-step-lesson-jinja/s1]
---

{{ raw }} kept.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-step-lesson-jinja/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-step-lesson-jinja
title: Step Lesson Jinja
summary: A step lesson on a Jinja playbook.
jinja: true
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-step-lesson-jinja/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  s1: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-step-lesson-jinja/s1/prompt.md --
---
name: s1
summary: Only step.
detached: sonnet:medium
---

Step body sees {{ config.core.fx_label }}.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-step-lesson-jinja --step s1
-- exit --
0
